  "answer": "Yes, other users have already requested this feature. It's a HazeOver-style tool that dims inactive windows. PowerToys#13035 is the main ticket, and #9496 and #15125 were closed as duplicates of it. The archive shows no built-in PowerToys feature yet. The discussion in #13035 only reached a proof-of-concept idea: a separate app with an underlay that has a colour and transparency setting. Add a 👍 reaction to #13035 and include your requirements there: adjustable dimming intensity and multi-monitor support. Until a feature ships, the tickets mention these third-party Windows options: PowerDimmer (github.com/[user]/PowerDimmer), LeDimmer, and FocusDim (getpeakflow.pro/focusdim). FocusDim's author posted it in #9496 and #15125, so it is a self-promoted product. Check any of them yourself before relying on it."
